            model3DHotspots: [], customLightNames: {}, author: "",
            drivingExperience: "The 204hp DTPA is an evolution of the 40 TDI, updated for the strict Euro 6e emissions standards. It offers a fantastic balance of power and economy. The 400 Nm of torque combined with the seamless 12V MHEV stop-start system makes city driving effortless, while the excellent NVH insulation means the diesel clatter is virtually nonexistent inside the cabin. On the highway, it settles into a remarkably quiet, low-rpm cruise, returning excellent fuel economy.",
            mechanicVerdict: "The DTPA EA288evo is a very strong and reliable engine mechanically, but you are buying into significant emissions complexity—specifically the Twin-Dosing SCR system. The 12V BAS system and the switchable water pump are your main points of mechanical failure, while the dual AdBlue injectors are virtually guaranteed to need repairs as the car ages. Fortunately, it doesn't suffer from the catastrophic flaws of older VW diesels. If you properly maintain the emissions systems and fix the water pump, it's a solid 400,000+ km engine.",
            repairCostEstimate: "$800 - $1500 / year (Mechanically solid, but Twin-Dosing SCR/AdBlue sensor failures or a sticking water pump can cause sudden, moderate repair bills)"
