            model3DHotspots: [], customLightNames: {}, author: "",
            drivingExperience: "The 344hp DMKC S6 TDI continues the legacy of the European diesel S6. The inclusion of the 48V Electric Powered Compressor (EPC) eliminates diesel turbo lag entirely; step on the gas, and 700 Nm of torque hits you instantly, throwing you into the seat. It is an unstoppable, relentless wave of power. The ZF 8-speed shifts smoothly, and the active exhaust gives it a surprisingly aggressive rumble. It is the ultimate Autobahn missile, offering V8-like performance with diesel fuel economy.",
            mechanicVerdict: "The DMKC S6 TDI's engine block is a masterpiece, but the electronics surrounding it are terrifying. The 48V BAS (Belt Alternator Starter) generator fails constantly, leaving owners completely stranded with a dead car. Furthermore, the CP4 fuel pump remains a constant threat, and the EPC adds another layer of highly expensive complexity. If you buy this car, a comprehensive warranty is strongly recommended. When it works, it is an engineering marvel, but a 48V failure is a 'when', not an 'if'.",
            repairCostEstimate: "$1500 - $3500+ / year (High risk. A 48V BAS failure is an instant $2000+ repair, and CP4 fuel pump failure is a catastrophic expense)"
