            model3DHotspots: [], customLightNames: {}, author: "",
            drivingExperience: "The 204hp DMSB 40 TFSI provides a beautifully refined, modern executive experience for the C9 generation. The 12V Mild Hybrid system smooths out the stop-start function seamlessly. The high-compression B-Cycle engine delivers its 340 Nm of torque effortlessly, making the car feel agile in city traffic. It is exceptionally quiet and paired with the DL382 transmission, it offers incredibly responsive daily performance.",
            mechanicVerdict: "The EA888 Gen 4 'evo4' is a masterpiece of efficiency, but it brings complexities. The core block is phenomenally reliable. However, you are still dealing with the classic plastic water pump module, which WILL leak and warp. Furthermore, dropping MPI means you must budget for walnut blasting the intake valves around 100k km. If you replace the water pump proactively, maintain the PCV valve, and strictly adhere to DSG fluid changes, this engine is an incredibly solid daily driver.",
            repairCostEstimate: "$600 - $1200 / year (Highly reliable, but replacing the inevitable leaking water pump module is an expensive, labor-intensive job)"
