            timingType: "Chain (EA888 Gen 4 architecture. Features an incredibly robust timing chain system, practically eliminating the stretch issues of early 2.0 TFSI generations. High-mileage monitoring is still standard practice).", injectionType: "Direct Injection (FSI exclusively. The Gen 4 engine increases fuel pressure to a massive 350 bar to improve atomization and emissions, dropping the dual injection of Gen 3).", engineLifespan: "300,000+ km (The ultimate iteration of the 4-cylinder EA888. The core block is practically unburstable. Lifespan is primarily dictated by the maintenance of plastic cooling components and the MHEV system).", turboType: "Single Turbocharger (Continental/IHI variant. Highly optimized for the high-output mapping, providing rapid spool and sustained top-end power).", ecuType: "Bosch MG1 (Highly advanced engine management system orchestrating the Belt Alternator Starter, OPF, and the 350 bar injection system).", euroStandard: "Euro 6e", maxPowerStockInternals: "420+ hp (The Gen 4 block and internals are phenomenally strong. Highly receptive to larger turbo swaps without opening the engine).",
            fuelConsumption: { city: "8.5 - 9.5 L/100km", highway: "5.8 - 6.8 L/100km", mixed: "6.8 - 7.8 L/100km", sporty: "11.0+ L/100km" },
            oilSpecification: "VW 508.00 0W-20",
            commonIssues: [ 
                "Thermostat & Water Pump Housing Leaks: Despite being Gen 4, the plastic housing still warps and cracks under constant thermal cycling, causing slow coolant loss.",
                "PCV Valve Failure: The internal rubber diaphragm tears, leading to vacuum leaks, rough idle, whistling noises, and increased crankcase pressure.",
                "12V BAS (Belt Alternator Starter) Wear: The mild-hybrid starter generator places extra stress on the serpentine belt and its internal bearings can wear out.",
                "OPF (Otto Particulate Filter) Sensors: The differential pressure sensors for the exhaust particulate filter can fail, throwing emissions codes.",
                "Intake Valve Carbon Buildup: Because Gen 4 dropped MPI (Multi-Point Injection), the intake valves are once again susceptible to carbon buildup over high mileage.",
                "S Tronic Mechatronic Wear: The DL382 7-speed dual-clutch transmission can experience harsh shifting if 60,000 km fluid changes are ignored."
            ],
            vulnerabilities: [ 
                "Catastrophic Overheating - The plastic water pump module can fail suddenly, rapidly dumping coolant and warping the aluminum cylinder head before the driver notices.",
                "Rear Main Seal Blowout - A failed PCV valve permanently pressurizes the engine crankcase, which eventually blows out the rear main seal, causing massive oil leaks.",
                "MHEV System Lockout - If the 12V Lithium-Ion battery in the rear or the BAS unit fails, the car may refuse to start or charge the primary 12V system.",
                "Transmission Destruction - The 7-speed S Tronic DL382 gearbox will suffer catastrophic clutch pack and mechatronic failure without strict fluid and filter services.",
                "Airflow Choking (Carbon) - Without walnut blasting, the FSI-only injection will eventually choke the intake valves with carbon, causing misfires and power loss.",
                "Coolant Migration - Defective coolant temperature sensors can leak coolant internally into the wiring harness, migrating all the way to the ECU and destroying it."
            ],
