                "OPF (Otto Particulate Filter) Sensors: The differential pressure sensors for the exhaust particulate filter can fail, throwing emissions codes.",
                "PCV Valve Failure: The crankcase ventilation valve frequently fails, causing a loud whistle, increased oil consumption, and potential rear main seal damage.",
                "Water Pump & Thermostat Leaks: The complex thermal management module and water pump are prone to leaking coolant into the engine valley.",
                "S Tronic Mechatronic Wear: The DL382+ transmission requires strict fluid changes to handle the massive 550 Nm torque output."
