            drivingExperience: "The 362hp DLZA 55 TFSI is an incredibly refined and violently fast executive express. Thanks to the Hot-V turbo layout and the 48V mild-hybrid system, throttle response is instantaneous; the electric motor fills in the torque gaps before the turbo fully spools. It completely masks the weight of the C9 chassis, pulling with a relentless, linear surge to the redline. Paired with the DL382+ S Tronic, it offers the perfect duality of absolute highway silence and genuine sports-sedan aggression.",
            mechanicVerdict: "The EA839 3.0 TFSI is a powerhouse. The C9 generation resolves the terrifying rocker arm defect of the early C8s, making the block itself virtually bulletproof. However, you are still dealing with the nightmare of the 48V BAS generator failing and leaving you stranded, plus the highly restrictive Euro 6e OPF filters which complicate tuning. If you proactively manage the cooling system leaks in the Hot-V and keep a repair fund ready for the 48V alternator, this is an astonishingly capable engine.",
