            drivingExperience: "The 367hp DRYA 55 TFSI e provides an incredible dual-personality driving experience. In EV mode, it glides in absolute silence through city traffic. When you pin the throttle, the ICE kicks in seamlessly, and the combined 500 Nm of torque provides a powerful, V6-rivalling surge. However, the immense weight of the hybrid battery pack is highly noticeable in corners, making it a straight-line Autobahn cruiser rather than a canyon carver.",
            mechanicVerdict: "The DRYA pairs the incredibly robust EA888 Gen 4 engine block with a highly complex High-Voltage electrical system. The engine block itself is sound (though dropping MPI brings back carbon buildup concerns), but the hybrid integration adds terrifying repair bills if things go wrong. The electric A/C compressor remains a widely known failure point that will instantly brick the hybrid system. Great when it works perfectly, but extremely expensive when it breaks.",
